  "family": "focus-and-replay",
  "description": "The state produced by the story — the initial claim (●) and the additional claim (◆), which travelled the opposite way, both standing in the case-file rack, and the calendar marking the additional claim’s supplied day — with the supplied texts in a column. A lens opens beside the rack: a real enlarged copy of the rack and the calendar at the same coordinates, with a datum card. Inside the lens only the supplied day changes — the calendar mark moves to the alternative day; both claims stay where they are — then the context takes the same change, with a Δ changed-datum marker. Seeking back restores the old datum. No rule, requirement, time limit or effect of a day is shown.",
